# Fix code, not Controller (default)

When Contoller jobs fail on chad/dev AAP, **fix the problem in `infra.ado` / preflight-ui / bootstrap seeds** so the next bootstrap run generates correct artifacts. Do **not** work around failures by editing live AAP, OpenShift, or the generated bootstrap repo by hand and re-launching JTs - unless the user **explicitly** says to skip the code path.

## Hard rule

| Do | Do not (unless user explicitly asks) |
|----|--------------------------------------|
| Diagnose job stdout → find root cause in collection/roles/env gen | `oc patch`, manual secret/CR edits, survey hotfixes on Controller |
| Fix roles, `bootstrap_generate_env_vars`, playbooks, JTs, preflight UI | Re-launch failed JTs and call it "fixed" |
| Build collection tarball → copy into preflight `collections/` | SSH into cluster and "fix forward" without a code change |
| Tell the **user** the steps to redeploy and re-bootstrap | Run bootstrap, project sync, or JT launches for the user |

Use AAP/OCP API and `oc` only for **diagnosis** (read job stdout, inspect CR status), not as the delivery path for permanent fixes.

## Agent deliverable after a code fix

1. Code + changelog (+ README/lint per check-in gate).
2. Build and copy tarball (agent may run build/copy; user runs preflight deploy):

```bash
cd /home/chelliot/openshift/git/github-ado/ado
ansible-galaxy collection build -o /tmp
cp /tmp/infra-ado-*.tar.gz ../ado-preflight-ui/collections/
```

3. Give the user this checklist - **do not substitute running it yourself**:

### User steps (local preflight)

```bash
cd /home/chelliot/openshift/git/github-ado/ado-preflight-ui
./restart_pod.sh
# Open http://127.0.0.1:8080 - import ~/Downloads/ado-preflight-*.json, submit bootstrap
# Wait for recap (poll logs / bootstrap/result)
```

### User steps (OpenShift preflight - prod portal)

After tarball is in `collections/`, rebuild/push preflight image and rollout (same as `restart_pod.sh` path for OCP). Hard-refresh browser. Re-run bootstrap from the portal UI.

### User steps (after bootstrap succeeds)

1. **Git push** generated bootstrap repo (if preflight did not auto-push).
2. **Controller** → `DEV-project` (or your org project) → **Sync** (allow ≥600s first time).
3. Confirm `collections/requirements.yml` in bootstrap repo references the new `infra-ado-*.tar.gz` if vendored.
4. **Re-launch** failed workflow/JTs (or full OpenShift workflow) - user runs this, not the agent.

## When user says "just fix it in AAP"

Only then may the agent apply live cluster/Controller changes - and still follow up with the proper code fix in the same effort when the workaround reveals a real bug.

